</g></g><g stroke-width="0.85pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 167.27 L 52.58 167.27 L 52.58 266.99 L 12.03 266.99"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 -0.00002 0.00002 -1.0 15.32 266.99)"><path d="M 7.88 0 L 1.9 2.22 L 3.58 0 L 1.9 -2.22 Z"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span><span id="S2.F1.sf4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Normalization layer placements in various architectures.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we study six major schemes: <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al.,, 2017</a>)</cite>, <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al.,, 2020</a>)</cite>, <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim, B., Johnson, M. et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>, and <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al.,, 2025</a>)</cite>. Note that <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> is a combination of <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> for <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> for <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math> while LayerNorm-Scaling (<span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span>) is a deterministic rescaling of <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>. The four remaining schemes are presented in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.2 Normalization. ‣ 2 Normalized Attention Dynamics ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Such explicitly layer-normalization rules are not the only strategies employed in practice. Other attempts to improve normalization suggest better initializations <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{0},K^{0},V^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{0},K^{0},V^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kedia et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite> and explicit scaling of the updates, similarly to <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that is trainable in <span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thanks to the residual connections, each layer-update can be seen as a forward Euler discretization of a continuous-time ODE that captures the dynamics of tokens while enabling the deployment of useful calculus tools. In this context, it is convenient to write <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of time and replace <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}-X^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}-X^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. For any two matrices <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> has unit-norm columns, define the projection operator <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{X}Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{X}Y</annotation></semantics></math> to be the column-wise projection on to the tangent space of the sphere <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{X}Y=\big[\mathbf{P}_{x_{1}}y_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{P}_{x_{n}}y_{n}\big]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{X}Y=\big[\mathbf{P}_{x_{1}}y_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{P}_{x_{n}}y_{n}\big]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where for any <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1},y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1},y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{x}y=y-\langle y,x\rangle x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{x}y=y-\langle y,x\rangle x</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> onto the tangent space of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The dynamics described by each normalization schemes are presented in Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 2.2 Normalization. ‣ 2 Normalized Attention Dynamics ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Normalization Schemes in Discrete and Continuous Time Domains. In <span id="S2.T1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>, <math id="S2.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a layer-dependent learnable parameter.</figcaption>
<table id="S2.T1.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T1.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scheme</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S2.T1.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discrete Time Update</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S2.T1.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continuous Time Update</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.T1.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=X^{t}+A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=X^{t}+A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t))\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t))\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=\big[\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=\big[\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=\big[\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=\big[\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top"></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phantom{X^{t+1}}+\big[X^{t}+A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t})\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phantom{X^{t+1}}+\big[X^{t}+A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t})\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phantom{\dot{X}(t)}+\big[A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t))\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phantom{\dot{X}(t)}+\big[A^{t}\bigl(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t))\bigr)\big]{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=X^{t}+\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(A^{t}(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t}))\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=X^{t}+\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(A^{t}(\mathsf{Norm}(X^{t}))\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(A^{t}(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t)))\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(A^{t}(\mathsf{Norm}(X(t)))\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+\alpha_{t}\,\mathsf{Norm}(A^{t}(X^{t}))\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+\alpha_{t}\,\mathsf{Norm}(A^{t}(X^{t}))\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}\alpha_{t}\mathsf{Norm}(A^{t}(X(t)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}\alpha_{t}\mathsf{Norm}(A^{t}(X(t)))</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:51.7pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.T1.4.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{t+1}=\mathsf{Norm}\bigl(X^{t}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}A^{t}(X^{t})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="S2.T1.4.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{X}(t)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{X}(t)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+1}}\mathbf{P}_{X(t)}A^{t}(X(t))</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.3  Speed regulation formulation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>, <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>, and <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span>, tokens are constrained to the the sphere <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span> simply adjusting the speed of the particles as a function of <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> compared to <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>. For the other rules where tokens may have varying magnitude, one final projection is typically applied before the final decoding layer in practice. In particular, this means that decoding depends on <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">directions</em> <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}(t)=\mathsf{Norm}(x_{j}(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}(t)=\mathsf{Norm}(x_{j}(t))</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Interestingly, when tracking only the directional components
<math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}(t),\ldots,\theta_{n}(t)\in\mathcal{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}(t),\ldots,\theta_{n}(t)\in\mathcal{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
all normalization rules give rise to interacting particle systems
evolving on the sphere, governed by a common velocity field but subject
to distinct, rule-dependent speed-regulation mechanisms.
Note that this does not imply the particles follow the same trajectories
at different speeds; indeed the speed parameter has a significant impact on the trajectories. More specifically, directions <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{n}\in{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{n}\in{\mathcal{S}}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> undergo the <em id="S2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">normalized attention dynamics</em> given by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\dot{\theta}_{j}(t)=\frac{1}{s_{j}(t)}\,\mathbf{P}_{\theta_{j}(t)}\,A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\;}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\dot{\theta}_{j}(t)=\frac{1}{s_{j}(t)}\,\mathbf{P}_{\theta_{j}(t)}\,A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\;}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(NA)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(t)=[\theta_{1}(t),\ldots,\theta_{n}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(t)=[\theta_{1}(t),\ldots,\theta_{n}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math> and we recall that <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\theta}=I_{d}-\theta\theta^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\theta}=I_{d}-\theta\theta^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection from <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to the tangent space of the sphere at <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the following identities</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{r}_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{r}_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\theta_{j}(t),\dot{x}_{j}(t)\rangle\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\theta_{j}(t),\dot{x}_{j}(t)\rangle\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\theta}_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\theta}_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{r_{j}(t)}\big(\dot{x}_{j}(t)-\dot{r}_{j}(t)\theta_{j}(t)\big)=\frac{1}{r_{j}(t)}\mathbf{P}_{\theta_{j}(t)}\dot{x}_{j}(t)\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{r_{j}(t)}\big(\dot{x}_{j}(t)-\dot{r}_{j}(t)\theta_{j}(t)\big)=\frac{1}{r_{j}(t)}\mathbf{P}_{\theta_{j}(t)}\dot{x}_{j}(t)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">we readily get:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Speed regulation factors</figcaption>
<table id="S2.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S2.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
