<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Symmetric initialization</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section supplements the results of Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Prelude: Symmetric initialization ‣ 4 Initial and terminal token velocities ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> by establishing the ODE governing the evolution of cosine similarity <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and the magnitude <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for each normalization scheme. While Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 Asymptotic clustering ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> guarantees convergence to a point mass from almost all initial configurations, we need to ensure that <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> from a symmetric initialization as it approximates a random initial configuration when the embedding dimension <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is large. Below, the ODEs governing the evolution of <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, that is the form of <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)=2\langle\dot{\theta}_{k}(t),\theta_{1}(t)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)=2\langle\dot{\theta}_{k}(t),\theta_{1}(t)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> can be derived using basic substitutions and we omit these details. Moreover, since, <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> is simply a combination of <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> and <span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>, the initial and terminal velocity in this case follow directly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>. The ODE governing the evolution of the cosine similarity <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> was already derived in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al.,, 2025</a>, Theorem 6.8)</cite>. It is given by</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and it is known from the aforementioned theorem that <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact we readily see from the ODE that <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing. Writing <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon(t)=1-\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon(t)=1-\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\varepsilon}(t)\sim-2\varepsilon(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\varepsilon}(t)\sim-2\varepsilon(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. It yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{e^{\beta}+n-1}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}Ce^{-2t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{e^{\beta}+n-1}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}Ce^{-2t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>. The ODEs governing <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}(t)=\frac{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}\gamma(t)+e^{\beta}}{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}(t)=\frac{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}\gamma(t)+e^{\beta}}{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{r(t)((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{r(t)((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing so <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\geq\gamma(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\geq\gamma(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all positive <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)ne^{\beta}}(1-\gamma(t))\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)ne^{\beta}}(1-\gamma(t))\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">By Grönwall’s inequality, we get</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">exp</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">But since <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)\leq t+r(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)\leq t+r(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> and, in turn, <math id="A1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> so that<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          For two function <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\{0,\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\{0,\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="footnote1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a(t)\sim_{t\to T}b(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)\sim_{t\to T}b(t)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="footnote1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(t)/b(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)/b(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="footnote1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> <math id="A1.p5.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}t</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> by l’Hôpital’s rule.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Writing <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon(t)=1-\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon(t)=1-\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\varepsilon}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}-2\varepsilon(t)/r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}-2\varepsilon(t)/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\varepsilon}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}-2\varepsilon(t)/r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}-2\varepsilon(t)/t</annotation></semantics></math>. It yields that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{r(0)(e^{\beta}+n-1)}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}\frac{C}{t^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{r(0)(e^{\beta}+n-1)}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}\frac{C}{t^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span>. The ODEs governing <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}(t)=\frac{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}\gamma(t)+e^{\beta}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}(t)=\frac{(n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}\gamma(t)+e^{\beta}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{r(t)\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{r(t)\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The argument follows the same lines as for <span id="A1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>. Indeed, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)e^{\beta}\sqrt{1+(n-1)^{2}}}(1-\gamma(t))\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)ne^{\beta}}(1-\gamma(t))\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)e^{\beta}\sqrt{1+(n-1)^{2}}}(1-\gamma(t))\geq\frac{2e}{r(t)ne^{\beta}}(1-\gamma(t))\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">exp</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\frac{\mathrm{d}s}{r(s)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.5" class="ltx_p">To show that <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> in this case too, we employ a coarser approximation that is sufficient for our purpose:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}(t)\leq\frac{ne^{\beta}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\leq n\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}(t)\leq\frac{ne^{\beta}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\leq n\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.6" class="ltx_p">It readily yields that <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and in turn that <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}t</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{r(0)\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}\frac{C}{t^{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{r(0)\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}\frac{C}{t^{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>. The ODE governing <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2\alpha_{t}e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}},." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2\alpha_{t}e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+2(n-1)e^{\beta(1+\gamma(t))}\gamma(t)+(n-1)e^{2\beta\gamma(t)}(1+(n-2)\gamma(t))}},.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">This is the same formula as <span id="A1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span> where <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced with <math id="A1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}\mathrm{d}s\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">exp</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\gamma(t)\leq\mathop{\rm exp}\left(-\frac{2e}{ne^{\beta}}\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}\mathrm{d}s\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Assuming that <math id="A1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen such that the above integral diverges as <math id="A1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that <math id="A1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. It yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2\alpha_{0}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}C\alpha_{t}e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}\mathrm{d}s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2\alpha_{0}}{\sqrt{e^{2\beta}+n-1}}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}C\alpha_{t}e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}\mathrm{d}s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span>. The ODE governing <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{\sqrt{t+1}((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)=\frac{2e^{\beta\gamma(t)}(1-\gamma(t))((n-1)\gamma(t)+1)}{\sqrt{t+1}((n-1)e^{\beta\gamma(t)}+e^{\beta})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Observe that the cosine similarity evolves precisely as (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In Appendix A Symmetric initialization ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) but with predetermined magnitude <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(t)=\sqrt{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(t)=\sqrt{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we get that <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. We readily get</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{e^{\beta}+n-1}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}C\frac{e^{-4\sqrt{t}}}{\sqrt{t}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></msup><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to 0}\frac{2}{e^{\beta}+n-1}\,,\qquad\dot{\gamma}(t)\sim_{t\to\infty}C\frac{e^{-4\sqrt{t}}}{\sqrt{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem 4.2</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we prove an upper bound on the initial attention vector. Assume <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\log n\geq d\geq\log^{2}n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\log n\geq d\geq\log^{2}n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Q^{\top}K\|_{\mathrm{op}},\|V\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Q^{\top}K\|_{\mathrm{op}},\|V\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.i.d. random uniform <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left(\forall j\in[n]\,\|A_{j}(\Theta(0))\|\leq C\frac{\log n}{d}\right)\geq 1-n^{-C}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left(\forall j\in[n]\,\|A_{j}(\Theta(0))\|\leq C\frac{\log n}{d}\right)\geq 1-n^{-C}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout this proof, <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a universal constant that may change from line to line.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix token <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>—without loss of generality, <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=n</annotation></semantics></math>—and work conditionally on <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the random variables:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{k}:=\theta_{n}^{\top}Q^{\top}K\theta_{k}\,,\quad k=1,\ldots,n\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}:=\theta_{n}^{\top}Q^{\top}K\theta_{k}\,,\quad k=1,\ldots,n\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our goal is to control the norm of the vector</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(\Theta(0)):=V\frac{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{X_{k}}\theta_{k}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{X_{k}}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(\Theta(0)):=V\frac{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{X_{k}}\theta_{k}}{\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{X_{k}}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since we assume that <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|V\|_{op}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|V\|_{op}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we may assume without loss of generality that <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=I_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=I_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability vector given by <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\propto e^{X_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\propto e^{X_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and observe that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}w_{k}\theta_{k}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\big(w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big)\theta_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}w_{k}\theta_{k}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}+\sum_{k=1}^{n}\big(w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big)\theta_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since the <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>s are i.i.d. centered and subGaussian with variance proxy <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C/d</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that with probability at least <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-n^{-C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-n^{-C}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{{n}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{{n}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, observe that for any <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\mathbb{E}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq\frac{C}{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\mathbb{E}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq\frac{C}{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, by vector Hoeffding, with probability at least <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-n^{-C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-n^{-C}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq\frac{C}{d}+C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}X_{k}\theta_{k}\big\|\leq\frac{C}{d}+C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">because we assumed <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\log n\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\log n\geq d</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now control the third and last term in the right-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem 4.2 ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
and observe that <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic and with norm at most 1. For <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the random variables <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d centered and subGaussian with variance proxy <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C/d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C/d</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence there exists an event <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-n^{-C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-n^{-C}</annotation></semantics></math>, on which</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{k\leq n-1}|X_{k}|\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{d}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{k\leq n-1}|X_{k}|\leq C\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{d}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq e^{\sqrt{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq e^{\sqrt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>, on <math id="A2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds for all <math id="A2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|e^{X_{k}}-1-X_{k}|\leq C{\frac{\log n}{d}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|e^{X_{k}}-1-X_{k}|\leq C{\frac{\log n}{d}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, we have that <math id="A2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X_{n}|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X_{n}|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-1}\leq e^{X_{n}}\leq e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-1}\leq e^{X_{n}}\leq e</annotation></semantics></math>. Together, these bounds yield that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+X_{k}-C{\frac{\log n}{d}}}{n-1+e}\leq w_{k}\leq\frac{1+X_{k}+C{\frac{\log n}{d}}}{n-1+e^{-1}}\,,\quad k\leq n-1\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+X_{k}-C{\frac{\log n}{d}}}{n-1+e}\leq w_{k}\leq\frac{1+X_{k}+C{\frac{\log n}{d}}}{n-1+e^{-1}}\,,\quad k\leq n-1\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">so that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big|\leq C\frac{\log n}{nd}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big|\leq C\frac{\log n}{nd}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the fact that <math id="A2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, using similar arguments, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big|\leq 2\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big|\leq 2\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Put together, the last two displays yield</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big\|\sum_{k=1}^{n}\big(w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big)\theta_{k}\Big\|\leq C\frac{\log n}{d}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big\|\sum_{k=1}^{n}\big(w_{k}-\frac{1}{n}-\frac{X_{k}}{n}\big)\theta_{k}\Big\|\leq C\frac{\log n}{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">Combined together we get the claimed estimate.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem 4.3</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Denote average <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\theta}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\theta}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider variance of tokens</p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(t):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=1-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(t):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=1-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\dot{\theta}_{k}-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\dot{\theta}_{k}-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We immediately have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle=\langle\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}-n\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle=\langle\sum_{k=1}^{n}\theta_{k}-n\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\dot{\theta}_{j}\rangle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus</p>
<table id="A3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\dot{\theta}_{k}\rangle=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}A_{k}\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\dot{\theta}_{k}\rangle=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}A_{k}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Let’s decompose <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k}:=A_{k}-\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k}:=A_{k}-\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> to get</p>
<table id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}\bar{\theta}\rangle+\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}\delta_{k}\rangle=I_{1}+I_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}\bar{\theta}\rangle+\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},\frac{1}{s_{k}}P_{k}\delta_{k}\rangle=I_{1}+I_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">For the first term we write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{2}I_{1}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},P_{k}\bar{\theta}\rangle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\langle-\bar{\theta},\bar{\theta}-\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle\theta_{k}\rangle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{2}I_{1}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\langle\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta},P_{k}\bar{\theta}\rangle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\langle-\bar{\theta},\bar{\theta}-\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle\theta_{k}\rangle=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Each term in the sum is non-positive, thus we can bound</p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\max_{k}s_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})\geq\frac{n}{2}I_{1}\geq\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\max_{k}s_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})\geq\frac{n}{2}I_{1}\geq\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The sum itself can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-n\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2})=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-n\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}(\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}-\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle=n\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=n-n\mathcal{V}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle=n\|\bar{\theta}\|^{2}=n-n\mathcal{V}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. With a fixed sum of <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, the min/max sum of squares <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{k},\bar{\theta}\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is achieved when they are equal/spread out, which gives us</p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\max_{k}s_{k}}(-2\mathcal{V}+2n\mathcal{V}^{2})\geq I_{1}\geq\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}(-2\mathcal{V}+2\mathcal{V}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\max_{k}s_{k}}(-2\mathcal{V}+2n\mathcal{V}^{2})\geq I_{1}\geq\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}(-2\mathcal{V}+2\mathcal{V}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">For the second term, we first upper bound the length of <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{k}\delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{k}\delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this aim, consider</p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{i}\rangle-\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle=\langle\theta_{k},Q^{\top}K(\theta_{i}-\theta_{j})\rangle\leq\|\theta_{k}\|\|Q^{\top}K\|_{op}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{j}\|\leq\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{j}\|\leq\sqrt{2\delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{i}\rangle-\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle=\langle\theta_{k},Q^{\top}K(\theta_{i}-\theta_{j})\rangle\leq\|\theta_{k}\|\|Q^{\top}K\|_{op}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{j}\|\leq\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{j}\|\leq\sqrt{2\delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.11" class="ltx_p">Consequently,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{ne^{-\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}}\geq\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle}}{\sum_{t=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{t}\rangle}}\geq\frac{1}{ne^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{ne^{-\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}}\geq\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle}}{\sum_{t=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{t}\rangle}}\geq\frac{1}{ne^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Which implies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|w_{kj}-\frac{1}{n}\right|=\left|\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle}}{\sum_{t=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{t}\rangle}}-\frac{1}{n}\right|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|w_{kj}-\frac{1}{n}\right|=\left|\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{j}\rangle}}{\sum_{t=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{k},K\theta_{t}\rangle}}-\frac{1}{n}\right|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|P_{k}\delta_{k}\|=\|\sum_{j=1}^{n}(w_{kj}-\frac{1}{n})P_{k}\theta_{j}\|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sum_{j=1}^{n}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{n}\sqrt{\sum_{j}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|P_{k}\delta_{k}\|=\|\sum_{j=1}^{n}(w_{kj}-\frac{1}{n})P_{k}\theta_{j}\|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sum_{j=1}^{n}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|\leq\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{n}\sqrt{\sum_{j}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Finally, one has</p>
<table id="A3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}\|P_{k}\theta_{j}\|^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}(1-\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle^{2})\leq n-\frac{1}{n}(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}(1-\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle^{2})\leq n-\frac{1}{n}(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n(1-\langle\bar{\theta},\theta_{k}\rangle^{2})\leq n(1-(1-n\mathcal{V})^{2})\leq 2n^{2}\mathcal{V}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n(1-\langle\bar{\theta},\theta_{k}\rangle^{2})\leq n(1-(1-n\mathcal{V})^{2})\leq 2n^{2}\mathcal{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.15" class="ltx_p">Combined, we obtain an upper bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|I_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|I_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|\|P_{k}\delta_{k}\|\leq\frac{2}{n}\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{n}\sqrt{2n^{2}\mathcal{V}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{1}{s_{k}}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|\|P_{k}\delta_{k}\|\leq\frac{2}{n}\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\frac{1}{n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{n}\sqrt{2n^{2}\mathcal{V}}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{2\mathcal{V}}(\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2})^{1/2}=2\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\mathcal{V}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\sqrt{2\mathcal{V}}(\sum_{k=1}^{n}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2})^{1/2}=2\frac{1}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\mathcal{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we obtain upper and lower bounds on <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=I_{1}+I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)=I_{1}+I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{-2\mathcal{V}+2n\mathcal{V}^{2}}{\max_{k}s_{k}}+\frac{2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)}{\min_{k}s_{K}}\mathcal{V}\geq\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)\geq\frac{-2\mathcal{V}+2\mathcal{V}^{2}-2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{-2\mathcal{V}+2n\mathcal{V}^{2}}{\max_{k}s_{k}}+\frac{2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)}{\min_{k}s_{K}}\mathcal{V}\geq\mathcal{V}^{\prime}(t)\geq\frac{-2\mathcal{V}+2\mathcal{V}^{2}-2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let us also mention that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\delta=\max_{k,j}\|\theta_{k}-\theta_{j}\|^{2}\leq 4\max_{k}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2}\leq 4n\mathcal{V}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\delta=\max_{k,j}\|\theta_{k}-\theta_{j}\|^{2}\leq 4\max_{k}\|\theta_{k}-\bar{\theta}\|^{2}\leq 4n\mathcal{V},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">whereas</p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\mathcal{V}=\langle\bar{\theta},\bar{\theta}\rangle\geq 1-\delta,\;\textrm{i.e.}\;\mathcal{V}\leq\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>i.e.</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\mathcal{V}=\langle\bar{\theta},\bar{\theta}\rangle\geq 1-\delta,\;\textrm{i.e.}\;\mathcal{V}\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the true local rate of clustering that we get from bounds (<a href="#A3.E4" title="In Appendix C Proof of Theorem 4.3 ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is defined by the main terms on both sides <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-2\mathcal{V}/{\max_{k}s_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\mathcal{V}/{\max_{k}s_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-2\mathcal{V}/\min_{k}s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\mathcal{V}/\min_{k}s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, as <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min s_{k}\sim\max s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min s_{k}\sim\max s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we obtain a tight rate of convergence.
To establish the result we claimed, notice that for <math id="A3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;\frac{1}{100n^{2}\beta^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;\frac{1}{100n^{2}\beta^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> one has</p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\leq\frac{\sqrt{2}}{3\sqrt{n}},\qquad 2n\mathcal{V}^{2}\leq 2n\delta\mathcal{V}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{2n}(e^{\beta\sqrt{2\delta}}-1)\leq\frac{\sqrt{2}}{3\sqrt{n}},\qquad 2n\mathcal{V}^{2}\leq 2n\delta\mathcal{V},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">giving us</p>
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{-2+2n\delta+\sqrt{2}/(3\sqrt{n})}{\max_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}\geq\mathcal{V}^{\prime}\geq\frac{-2-\sqrt{2}/(3\sqrt{n})}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{-2+2n\delta+\sqrt{2}/(3\sqrt{n})}{\max_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}\geq\mathcal{V}^{\prime}\geq\frac{-2-\sqrt{2}/(3\sqrt{n})}{\min_{k}s_{k}}\mathcal{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we finish the proof with trivial estimates on <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, that follow from the fact that all products <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{k},\theta_{j}\rangle\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{k},\theta_{j}\rangle\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and definitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for <span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span> <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)^{3/2}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)^{3/2}t</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for <span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span> <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)^{1/2}\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)^{1/2}\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for <span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> <math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)(t-\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq s_{k}\geq(1-\delta)(t-\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for <span id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span> <math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}\equiv\sqrt{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}\equiv\sqrt{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Substituted into the estimate (<a href="#A3.E5" title="In Appendix C Proof of Theorem 4.3 ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we obtain the claimed rates.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremarkx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The true local rate of convergence of <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmremarkx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> that we get from equation (<a href="#A3.E4" title="In Appendix C Proof of Theorem 4.3 ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-2t(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-2t(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}ds(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\int_{0}^{t}\alpha_{s}ds(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-2\log t(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=e^{-4\sqrt{t}(1+o(1))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=e^{-4\sqrt{t}(1+o(1))}</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A3.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Final convergence</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we prove Theorem 3.1 from the main text, that claims that under some assumptions, for almost any initial configuration of particles, any normalized attention dynamics that we study (that is <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>, <span id="A4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> and <span id="A4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span>) converges to a single cluster. First, let us outline the core of the proof.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">D.1  Proof Outline for Token Synchronization in Pre-LN</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A conventional proof that all tokens converge to a single state consists of two stages. Showing that there is some limiting configuration of tokens, and then verifying that the only possible limiting configuration is the consensual one.
We follow the same approach, but at each step we introduce novel technical details due to our general point of view. For simplicity of exposition, in the outline we follow <span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Existence of a Limit Point</span>
First, we demonstrate that the token dynamics indeed converge to a limiting configuration. This step heavily depends on the system. Common approach leverages the Łojasiewicz inequality, as seen in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al., (2025)</a></cite>. It can be adopted to our setting, as we will show later. Moreover, our proof extends the gradient case <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\top}K=V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\top}K=V</annotation></semantics></math> to a more general case, extending the synchronization results by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al., (2025)</a></cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Criscitiello et al., (2024)</a></cite>, even in <span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Local behavior at the limiting point.</span>
Second, we must prove that any such limit point corresponds to the synchronized state where all tokens are identical. The classical argument involves a local stability analysis around the system’s critical points. One can typically show that any non-synchronized critical points are unstable and that their basin of attraction has measure zero, making them insignificant as final states. A comprehensive linearization analysis can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Criscitiello et al., (2024)</a></cite> that, in particular, covers <span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> dynamics with <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Together with a recent proof of synchronization for <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Polyanskiy et al., (2025)</a></cite>, the stability of <span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> system Jacobian is well-studied. We also rely on this method, but first we need to resolve the fact that <span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> system is non-compact.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transformation to compact state space.</span> The <span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> state-space is non-compact, because both empirically and theoretically tokens’ magnitude <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> grows to infinity with <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. This restricts the direct study of the limiting point in that space. We can transform it to a compact state space by the following trick, however. Consider a logarithmic time scale <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\ln t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\ln t</annotation></semantics></math> and modified scale variables <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}:=s_{j}/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}:=s_{j}/t</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying the chain rule, we find the transformed dynamics:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\theta_{j}}{d\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\theta_{j}}{d\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q_{j}}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q_{j}}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{dq_{j}}{d\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{dq_{j}}{d\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle-q_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle-q_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This formulation is interesting in its own right. It reveals that the <span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> system evolves on a logarithmic time scale, which may explain its observed stability advantages over <span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> variants in deep architectures. Furthermore, the dynamics are scaled by <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are driven toward <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, the alignment between a token and its attention vector.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially for our proof, this transformed system is still <span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">autonomous</span>. This allows us to proceed with the final step: a rigorous linearization analysis of its critical points. By showing that all critical points corresponding to non-consensual states are unstable in the <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta,q,\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta,q,\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> frame, we can conclude that the system must converge to the state where all tokens are identical.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In what follows we are going to cover all the proof steps in detail.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">D.2  Generalized gradient descent convergence</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we need to refine an important result of Łojasiewicz on convergence of gradient descent, so that it fits our problem setting. We follow an approach similar to the one presented in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haraux, (2012)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(t)</annotation></semantics></math> be a symmetric real matrix <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\lambda(t)I\succ M(t)\succ\lambda(t)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\lambda(t)I\succ M(t)\succ\lambda(t)I</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(t)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(t)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}\lambda(t)dt=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}\lambda(t)dt=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and some constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let energy function <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be analytic in an open set <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subset\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subset\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a compact path <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\subset U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\subset U</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies the following modified gradient descent equation</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}=-M(t)\nabla_{x}E(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}=-M(t)\nabla_{x}E(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> converges to a critical point of the energy function <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\to x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\to x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla E(x^{*})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla E(x^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step I. Change of time.</span><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text"> First, define a new time variable <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\lambda(s)ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(t)=\int_{0}^{t}\lambda(s)ds</annotation></semantics></math>. By assumption <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> monotonically grows to infinity as <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dx}{d\tau}=\frac{dx/dt}{d\tau/dt}=\frac{-M(t)\nabla_{x}E(x)}{\lambda(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx}{d\tau}=\frac{dx/dt}{d\tau/dt}=\frac{-M(t)\nabla_{x}E(x)}{\lambda(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{M}(\tau)=M(t(\tau))/\lambda(t(\tau))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{M}(\tau)=M(t(\tau))/\lambda(t(\tau))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dx}{d\tau}=-\tilde{M}(\tau)\nabla_{x}E(x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dx}{d\tau}=-\tilde{M}(\tau)\nabla_{x}E(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CI\succ\tilde{M}(\tau)\succ I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CI\succ\tilde{M}(\tau)\succ I</annotation></semantics></math>. This change of time proves that it is sufficient to prove the Lemma in its initial form under the assumption <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CI\succ M(t)\succ I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CI\succ M(t)\succ I</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(t)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to time change.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2.</span><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Now that we have <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CI\succ M(t)\succ I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CI\succ M(t)\succ I</annotation></semantics></math>, let us follow a known approach to the proof of gradient descent convergence.
Consider the energy along the trajectory, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t):=E(x(t))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t):=E(x(t)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)=(\dot{x})^{\top}\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)}=-(\dot{x})^{\top}M^{-1}\dot{x}\leq-C^{-1}|\dot{x}|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)=(\dot{x})^{\top}\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)}=-(\dot{x})^{\top}M^{-1}\dot{x}\leq-C^{-1}|\dot{x}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the energy is decreasing along the trajectory. Since <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded on a compact trajectory, we get that <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)\in L_{1}([0,\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)\in L_{1}([0,\infty))</annotation></semantics></math>. Because</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{x}|^{2}\leq C|f^{\prime}(t)|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{x}|^{2}\leq C|f^{\prime}(t)|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">we get that <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}\in L_{2}([0,\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}\in L_{2}([0,\infty))</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is an absolutely continuous function in <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}([0,\infty))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}([0,\infty))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, since <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(t)\succ cI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(t)\succ cI</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{x}E(x)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{x}E(x)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For convergence to a point this is not enough, but it already shows us that <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textrm{dist}(x,\mathcal{E})\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textrm{dist}(x,\mathcal{E})\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{a:\nabla E(a)=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{a:\nabla E(a)=0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, because the limit set <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> of a compact trajectory <math id="A4.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is compact and connected, we can use uniform Łojasiewicz inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">To get <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\to x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\to x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> we need to sharpen the estimate on <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is where the Łojasiewicz inequality is used.
It says that in some neighbourhood <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and some constants <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> one has</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E(u)-V|^{\alpha}\leq\|\nabla E(u)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E(u)-V|^{\alpha}\leq\|\nabla E(u)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">We can assume <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=0</annotation></semantics></math> by shifting the energy function. In particular, it means that <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)</annotation></semantics></math> decreases to 0 as <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, because <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> approaches <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that as <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> it is true that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E(x(t))|^{\alpha}\leq\|\nabla E(x(t))\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E(x(t))|^{\alpha}\leq\|\nabla E(x(t))\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, from our assumption <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(t)\succ I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(t)\succ I</annotation></semantics></math> we get</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t)=(\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)})^{\top}\dot{x}=-(\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)})^{\top}M(t)\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)}\leq-\|\nabla_{x}E(x(t))\|^{2}\leq-|f(t)|^{2\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t)=(\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)})^{\top}\dot{x}=-(\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)})^{\top}M(t)\nabla_{x}E|_{x(t)}\leq-\|\nabla_{x}E(x(t))\|^{2}\leq-|f(t)|^{2\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f^{1-2\alpha}(t))^{\prime}=(1-2\alpha)f^{-2\alpha}f^{\prime}\geq(2\alpha-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f^{1-2\alpha}(t))^{\prime}=(1-2\alpha)f^{-2\alpha}f^{\prime}\geq(2\alpha-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, for <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1/(2\alpha-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1/(2\alpha-1)</annotation></semantics></math> one has</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)\leq Kt^{-\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)\leq Kt^{-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">We know that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{x}|^{2}\leq C|f^{\prime}(t)|=-Cf^{\prime}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{x}|^{2}\leq C|f^{\prime}(t)|=-Cf^{\prime}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{t}^{2t}|\dot{x}|^{2}ds\leq C(f(t)-f(2t))\leq CKt^{-\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{t}^{2t}|\dot{x}|^{2}ds\leq C(f(t)-f(2t))\leq CKt^{-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">From this inequality and Cauchy-Schwarz we get</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{t}^{2t}|\dot{x}|ds\leq CKt^{(1-\beta)/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{t}^{2t}|\dot{x}|ds\leq CKt^{(1-\beta)/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, this estimate shows convergence of the path <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)</annotation></semantics></math> to some limiting point, because</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{1}^{\infty}|\dot{x}|\leq CK\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}2^{n(1-\beta)/2}&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{1}^{\infty}|\dot{x}|\leq CK\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}2^{n(1-\beta)/2}&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">D.3  Proof of Theorem 3.1</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix we provide a complete proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3 Asymptotic clustering ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. The argument follows the roadmap outlined in Section <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Proof Outline for Token Synchronization in Pre-LN ‣ Appendix D Final convergence ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, with minor adjustments for each normalization scheme. For simplicity of exposition, we first give a full analysis of <span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>. Then, we provide remarks on how to adapt the proof for each normalization scheme. Thanks to our unified formulation of normalization in (<a href="#S2.Ex5" title="In 2.3 Speed regulation formulation ‣ 2 Normalized Attention Dynamics ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">NA</span></a>), the core proof applies verbatim across all schemes—the only variation lies in some technical details. A forthcoming work will pursue that broader unification and extend the analysis beyond purely architectural speed regulators.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For convenience, let us recall the object of study. We consider the evolution of particles <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> on a unit sphere <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> governed by the ODE</p>
<table id="A4.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\theta}_{j}=\frac{1}{s_{j}}P_{j}A_{j},\qquad A_{j}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{j},K\theta_{k}\rangle}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{j},K\theta_{e}ll\rangle}}V\theta_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\theta}_{j}=\frac{1}{s_{j}}P_{j}A_{j},\qquad A_{j}=\sum_{k=1}^{n}\frac{e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{j},K\theta_{k}\rangle}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{n}e^{\beta\langle Q\theta_{j},K\theta_{e}ll\rangle}}V\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with normalization factor <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> evolving according to the following table.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Speed regulation factors</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"></th>
<th id="A4.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A4.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{r}_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{r}_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T3.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A4.T3.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A4.T3.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}+r_{j}(t){\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t\leq\tau}+r_{j}(t){\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\rangle{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.260em;" width="0.260em"><mn>1</mn></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\rangle{\rm 1}\kern-2.40005pt{\rm I}_{t&gt;\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A4.T3.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}(t)\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}(t)\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}(\theta_{j}(t))\rangle/\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{j}(t),A^{t}(\theta_{j}(t))\rangle/\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><span id="A4.T3.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{-1}\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{-1}\|A^{t}_{j}(\Theta(t))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T3.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T3.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T3.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span></th>
<td id="A4.T3.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T3.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider monotonically growing to infinity time change <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, normalized attention dynamics with speed regulation factors <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to normalized attention dynamics with speed regulation factors <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{j}(\tau)=s_{j}(t(\tau))/t^{\prime}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{j}(\tau)=s_{j}(t(\tau))/t^{\prime}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> in time <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This immediately follows from the definition</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\theta_{j}}{d\tau}=\frac{d\theta_{j}}{dt}t^{\prime}(\tau)=\frac{1}{s_{j}(t(\tau))/t^{\prime}(\tau)}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\theta_{j}}{d\tau}=\frac{d\theta_{j}}{dt}t^{\prime}(\tau)=\frac{1}{s_{j}(t(\tau))/t^{\prime}(\tau)}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This proposition shows that in the normalized attention dynamics we can divide <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by the same factor, as long as it’s positive and its inverse integrates to infinity. This notion helps us reduce time dependence in normalization dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 1. Time change</span><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider evolution starting at time <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> and a time change <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\ln t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\ln t</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt/d\tau=t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt/d\tau=t</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, set <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}(t):=r_{j}(t)/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}(t):=r_{j}(t)/t</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we rewrite <span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span> in time <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\theta}_{j}(\tau)=\frac{1}{q_{j}(\tau)}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta(\tau)),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}(\tau)=\langle\theta_{j}(\tau),A_{j}(\Theta(\tau))\rangle-q_{j}(\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\theta}_{j}(\tau)=\frac{1}{q_{j}(\tau)}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta(\tau)),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}(\tau)=\langle\theta_{j}(\tau),A_{j}(\Theta(\tau))\rangle-q_{j}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The function <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous and thus bounded on the compact. Then, all <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are upper bounded from the equation, and thus evolve on a segment <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,Q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,Q]</annotation></semantics></math>. This frame change is important, as it allows us to study an autonomous system on a compact, whereas in the original coordinates one usually has <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, the condition</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{j}\liminf_{t\to\infty}\dot{r}_{j}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{j}\liminf_{t\to\infty}\dot{r}_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">implies that all magnitudes <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are lower bounded by some linear function at <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, which translates into</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}(\tau)&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>τ</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}(\tau)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2. Gradient-like structure.</span><span id="A4.SS3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text">
We consider the event <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is enough to show synchronization under this assumption to prove the result.
First, to show the convergence of the system to some limiting configuration of angles <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.2 Generalized gradient descent convergence ‣ Appendix D Final convergence ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. For any trajectory <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> we can write</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\theta}_{j}=-\frac{1}{q_{j}Z_{j}}\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\theta}_{j}=-\frac{1}{q_{j}Z_{j}}\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">with spherical gradient of the following energy function</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E(\Theta)=-\frac{1}{2\beta}\sum_{j,k}e^{\beta\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(\Theta)=-\frac{1}{2\beta}\sum_{j,k}e^{\beta\langle\theta_{j},\theta_{k}\rangle}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">To get convergence of a specific trajectory <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> to some critical point <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to verify that the time-dependent matrix <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> with diagonal blocks <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{q_{j}Z_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{q_{j}Z_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the assumptions of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.2 Generalized gradient descent convergence ‣ Appendix D Final convergence ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. This is true, because the blocks are uniformly bounded. Indeed, the function <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded as continuous functions on a compact. Whereas <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are uniformly bounded on any trajectory we consider, with <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 3. Local behavior</span><span id="A4.SS3.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text">
We consider the event <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{j}\inf_{\tau}q_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\tau)\to\Theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\tau)\to\Theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to show that when the limiting point is not <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1}^{*}=\ldots=\theta_{n}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1}^{*}=\ldots=\theta_{n}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, this event has probability zero.
We can split the event into a countable union with assumptions <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{q_{j}(\tau)\geq\frac{1}{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{j}(\tau)\geq\frac{1}{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\inf_{j}\inf q_{j}&gt;0\}\subset\bigcup_{m\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}}\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall\tau&gt;0\;q_{j}\geq\frac{1}{m}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⊂</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\inf_{j}\inf q_{j}&gt;0\}\subset\bigcup_{m\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}}\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall\tau&gt;0\;q_{j}\geq\frac{1}{m}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">As we already mentioned, <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded from above. This means that under the restriction <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\geq\frac{1}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\geq\frac{1}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the combined state space of <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Theta,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Theta,q)</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact manifold. Our goal is to show that the event</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall t&gt;0\;q_{j}&gt;\frac{1}{m}\}\cup\{\forall j\in[n]\;\theta_{j}\to\theta_{j}^{*}\,|\,\Theta^{*}\textrm{is not synchronized}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext>is not synchronized</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall t&gt;0\;q_{j}&gt;\frac{1}{m}\}\cup\{\forall j\in[n]\;\theta_{j}\to\theta_{j}^{*}\,|\,\Theta^{*}\textrm{is not synchronized}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">has probability zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">When we get an autonomous dynamical system on a compact manifold, and we study its convergence to a limiting point, we need to study the Jacobian at that limiting point. Specifically, a well-known stability argument that was already written down several times (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Criscitiello et al., (2024)</a></cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al.,, 2025</a>, Lemma A.1)</cite>), employs central manifold theorem to show that basin of attraction of unstable critical points has measure zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">This argument applies to our case. Therefore, we move on to studying stability of critical points in the next part.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 4. Unstable direction of the </span><math id="A4.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS3.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> part</span><span id="A4.SS3.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the dynamics in the form</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\theta}_{j}=-\frac{1}{q_{j}(\tau)g_{j}(\Theta)}\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}=f_{j}(\Theta)-q_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\theta}_{j}=-\frac{1}{q_{j}(\tau)g_{j}(\Theta)}\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}=f_{j}(\Theta)-q_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}=Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}=Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}=\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}=\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A4.SS3.p12.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>.
In order to show that all limiting points <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Theta^{*},q^{*}),q^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Theta^{*},q^{*}),q^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that are not fully synchronized (i.e. not all <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are equal) have measure zero basin of attraction, we only need to check that they are all unstable. More specifically, that the Jacobian matrix at any such point <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{*},q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{*},q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> has an eigenvalue with a positive real part. Because of the specific form of our system, the Jacobian has a convenient block form</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J=\begin{pmatrix}J_{qq}&amp;J_{q\theta}\\
J_{\theta q}&amp;J_{\theta\theta}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J=\begin{pmatrix}J_{qq}&amp;J_{q\theta}\\
J_{\theta q}&amp;J_{\theta\theta}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{qq}=-I_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{qq}=-I_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\theta q}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\theta q}=0</annotation></semantics></math> because at the critical point <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta^{*})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{j}}E(\Theta^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, it is enough to show that <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\theta\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\theta\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> has a positive eigenvalue. Because of the gradient-like structure, <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\theta\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\theta\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the product of two matrices – <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{diag}(\frac{1}{f_{1}(\Theta^{*})g_{1}(\Theta^{*})},\ldots,\frac{1}{f_{n}(\Theta^{*})g_{n}(\Theta^{*})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{diag}(\frac{1}{f_{1}(\Theta^{*})g_{1}(\Theta^{*})},\ldots,\frac{1}{f_{n}(\Theta^{*})g_{n}(\Theta^{*})})</annotation></semantics></math> and a symmetric Hessian of the energy function <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. The Hessian itself is unstable, this is an established result due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Criscitiello et al., (2024)</a></cite> (for <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>) and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Polyanskiy et al., (2025)</a></cite> (for <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2</annotation></semantics></math>) that together closed synchronization for <span id="A4.SS3.p12.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Surprisingly, this is enough for our cause, because of the following matrix property, that shows the product of the diagonal matrix and unstable Hessian is again unstable. Note that the lemma is not true without the symmetry assumption on <math id="A4.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a symmetric unstable matrix <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and a symmetric positive-definite <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, the product <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DA</annotation></semantics></math> is also unstable.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, because <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric positive-definite, there is a symmetric positive-definite square root <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{2}=D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{2}=D</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consider a symmetric matrix <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=PAP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=PAP</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{-1}DAP=PAP=B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{-1}DAP=PAP=B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">thus matrices <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DA</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are similar, i.e. they share eigenvalues. On the other hand, by Sylvester’s law of inertia, <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> have the same inertia, and in particular the number of positive eigenvalues. Therefore, <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> has a positive eigenvalue, and so does <math id="A4.SS3.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DA</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 5. Basin of attraction of unstable critical points.</span><span id="A4.SS3.p15.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is well-known that the set of unstable critical points of a dynamical system on a compact has measure-zero basin of attraction (see for example <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al.,, 2025</a>, Lemma A.1)</cite> for a proof outline).
Thus, we obtain that the event</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall t&gt;0\;q_{j}&gt;\frac{1}{m}\}\cup\{\forall j\in[n]\;\theta_{j}\to\theta_{j}^{*}\,|\,\Theta^{*}\textrm{is not synchronized}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext>is not synchronized</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\forall j\in[n]\;\forall t&gt;0\;q_{j}&gt;\frac{1}{m}\}\cup\{\forall j\in[n]\;\theta_{j}\to\theta_{j}^{*}\,|\,\Theta^{*}\textrm{is not synchronized}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">has measure zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">For completeness, we include the proof here.
Let <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> be the flow for the system
<math id="A4.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{x}=F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{x}=F(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(\Theta,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(\Theta,q)</annotation></semantics></math>. The vector field <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth on the open domain where all <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any fixed <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the dynamics on the compact manifold</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}:=(S^{d-1})^{n}\times[1/m,Q]^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}:=(S^{d-1})^{n}\times[1/m,Q]^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">on which the flow is smooth. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m}\subseteq M_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m}\subseteq M_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the compact, forward-invariant set of initial conditions whose trajectories remain in <math id="A4.SS3.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ns}\subset K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ns}\subset K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of non-synchronized critical points.
By Step 4, every point <math id="A4.SS3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}\in S_{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}\in S_{ns}</annotation></semantics></math> is unstable.
Let <math id="A4.SS3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m,ns}\subset K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m,ns}\subset K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be the basin of attraction for <math id="A4.SS3.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ns}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the set of <math id="A4.SS3.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in K_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in K_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\tau\to\infty}\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})\in S_{ns}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\tau\to\infty}\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})\in S_{ns}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}\in S_{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}\in S_{ns}</annotation></semantics></math>, which lies in the interior of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Center-Stable Manifold Theorem applies.
It guarantees the existence of a local center-stable manifold <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The instability of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> implies that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathop{\rm dim}(W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}))\leq\mathop{\rm dim}(M_{m})-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathop{\rm dim}(W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}))\leq\mathop{\rm dim}(M_{m})-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> has measure zero. From the Center-Stable Manifold Theorem, there is a neighborhood of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> such that any trajectory staying in this neighborhood has to enter and remain on <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{cs}}^{\text{loc}}(x^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mtext>cs</mtext><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{cs}}^{\text{loc}}(x^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. By choosing a finite covering of the compact set <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ns}</annotation></semantics></math> with respective neighborhoods of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get that
any initial condition <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in A_{m,ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in A_{m,ns}</annotation></semantics></math> has a trajectory <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\tau}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> that must eventually enter and remain on some <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, with a finite number of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}_{k},k\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}_{k},k\leq K</annotation></semantics></math> chosen from the covering.
Thus, for some <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+},k\leq K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+},k\leq K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\Phi_{-N}(\Phi_{N}(x_{0})),\quad\text{where }\Phi_{N}(x_{0})\in W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\Phi_{-N}(\Phi_{N}(x_{0})),\quad\text{where }\Phi_{N}(x_{0})\in W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{-N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{-N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a local diffeomorphism, it preserves the dimensionality. Manifold <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mtext>loc</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\text{loc}}_{cs}(x^{*}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> has positive co-dimension, and thus its pre-image too, which implies that it has measure zero in <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, measure of <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m,ns}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m,ns}</annotation></semantics></math> is also zero, as a countable union of measure zero sets.
Finally, to completely finish, we need to map the set to <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>. This is again a smooth backward flow that preserves measure zero set. We arrive at measure zero set in initial coordinates <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Theta(0),r(0))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Theta(0),r(0))</annotation></semantics></math>, because they are distributed with standard Gaussian <math id="A4.SS3.p19.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(0)\cdot\Theta(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(0)\cdot\Theta(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremarkx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we describe modifications of the proof for each scheme.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span> No time change is required. The system is already autonomous and compact. <span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2</span> works with modified gradient descent from <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.2 Generalized gradient descent convergence ‣ Appendix D Final convergence ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, because the modification matrix <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal with blocks <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{Z_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{Z_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>, that are uniformly bounded. As such, we get convergence to some critical point. Finally, we use existing analysis of the stability of the energy functional together with <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 3.1 ‣ Appendix D Final convergence ‣ Normalization in Attention Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> to establish synchronization.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Peri-LN</span> For the <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 1</span> we use time change <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\ln t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\ln t</annotation></semantics></math> and also consider <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}(t):=r_{j}(t)/t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}(t):=r_{j}(t)/t</annotation></semantics></math>. It leads to the dynamics of the form</p>
<table id="A4.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\theta}_{j}=\frac{1}{q_{j}\|A_{j}(\Theta)\|}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}=\frac{\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle}{\|A_{j}(\Theta)\|}-q_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\theta}_{j}=\frac{1}{q_{j}\|A_{j}(\Theta)\|}P_{j}A_{j}(\Theta),\qquad\dot{q}_{j}=\frac{\langle\theta_{j},A_{j}(\Theta)\rangle}{\|A_{j}(\Theta)\|}-q_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The rest of the proof remains the same as <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>, because this system satisfies gradient-like structure of <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2</span>, we also use the assumption to separate <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and then show that all critical points that are not synchronized have unstable direction in <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 4</span>. The form of the system and the Jacobian in <span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 4</span> is written generally, to accommodate this case too.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> At infinity <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> follows exactly <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>, and the argument follows from the proof of <span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre-LN</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span> Time change <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\int\alpha_{t}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\int\alpha_{t}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> from <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 1</span> simplifies <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span> to the case <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>. This makes the original dynamics autonomous on a compact manifold. As such, it requires no frame change, and we immediately move on to studying convergence and local behavior of that system. Modified Łojasiewicz from <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 2</span> and analysis of the unstable direction of the Jacobian from <span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 4</span> follow similar steps. For the Jacobian, the only component is <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\theta\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\theta\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it is unstable from the same Lemma. The only complication for the system are points with <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. They, however, break the original dynamics too, and can be excluded with careful analysis.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span> Time change from <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Step 1</span> with <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=2\sqrt{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=2\sqrt{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LN-Scaling</span> to <span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-LN</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Simulation results with random weight matrices</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention Update Formulation.</span>
To align our simulations with practical transformer architectures, we now explicitly include the output projection matrix, <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, in the attention update. For a multi-head configuration, the output of each head <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is first computed and then concatenated, after which the final projection is applied:
<math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O_{h}=\text{softmax}(\beta XQ_{h}K_{h}^{T}X^{T})XV_{h},h=1,\ldots,n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>X</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{h}=\text{softmax}(\beta XQ_{h}K_{h}^{T}X^{T})XV_{h},h=1,\ldots,n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t+1}=\text{Concat}(O_{1},\ldots,O_{n_{\text{heads}}})W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t+1}=\text{Concat}(O_{1},\ldots,O_{n_{\text{heads}}})W</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h},K_{h},V_{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\text{head}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h},K_{h},V_{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\text{head}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The inclusion of the matrix <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear transformation applied after the core softmax-driven interaction. While this is crucial for model capacity in practice, it does not impact the theoretical dynamics description, which is why it was omitted from the preceding theoretical analysis for notational simplicity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental Settings.</span>
We present simulation results illustrating the evolution of average token cosine similarity. All plots show the mean trajectory averaged over <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> independent runs, with shaded regions indicating the 90% confidence interval. Each run begins with a fresh draw of initial token positions <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> from an isotropic distribution and random weight matrices. All simulations use a context of <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=128</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. For the normalization methods <span id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-LN</span> and <span id="A5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nGPT</span>, we use parameters <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.25T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.25T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our plots vary several factors.
The majority of our experiments use Kaiming initialization. In this setting, we fix the number of heads to <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{head}}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{head}}=d</annotation></semantics></math>) to isolate the core dynamics. We systematically vary the following parameters:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dimension (<math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: small (16), medium (128), and large (512).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Temperature (<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: low (<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>), medium (<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>), and high (<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=4\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=4\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weight Sampling</span>: <em id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">static</em> (a single draw of <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V,W</annotation></semantics></math> fixed for all time steps) vs. <em id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">re-sampled</em> (new matrices are drawn at each time step <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-style Initialization</span>: We conduct one experiment that mirrors the configuration of a small GPT-2 style model.</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It uses <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=768</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}=12</annotation></semantics></math> (implying <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{head}}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{head}}=64</annotation></semantics></math>), and a temperature of <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\sqrt{d_{\text{head}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>head</mtext></msub></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\sqrt{d_{\text{head}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Weights are drawn from a Gaussian distribution with variance <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and are held <em id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">static</em>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Figures are arranged to facilitate comparison, with each caption specifying the experimental signature <math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle d,n_{\text{heads}},\beta,\text{weights},\text{init}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>weights</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>init</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle d,n_{\text{heads}},\beta,\text{weights},\text{init}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A5.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.22026v1/figures/exp2_kaiming_h1_T10_midtemp.png" id="A5.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span><math id="A5.F5.sf1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A5.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">medium</span>), static Kaiming weights. Case where <math id="A5.F5.sf1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math>. </figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A5.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.22026v1/figures/exp3_kaiming_h1_T10_hightemp.png" id="A5.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><math id="A5.F5.sf2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=4\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=4\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="A5.F5.sf2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">high</span>), static Kaiming weights. Case where <math id="A5.F5.sf2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A5.F5.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.22026v1/figures/exp4_kaiming_h1_T10_regen.png" id="A5.F5.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span><math id="A5.F5.sf3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=512,n_{\text{heads}}=1,\beta=\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (medium), <span id="A5.F5.sf3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">re-sampled</span> Kaiming weights at each <math id="A5.F5.sf3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A5.F5.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.22026v1/figures/exp8_kaiming_overcomplete.png" id="A5.F5.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/298;" width="476" height="298" alt="Refer to caption">
